course: dictionary
lesson: 3910
title: Describing with frilly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frilly means decorated with frills, which are wavy strips of cloth or lace gathered into folds, as on a dress or a sock. «Some lie on the seabed looking like a frilly carpet.» A carpet with wavy, folded edges is what the author means, so frilly describes how something looks.
explain: Look at the words around frilly for clues. «Wobbegongs are flat sharks with patterned skin and frilly flaps around the mouth.» The flaps are wavy and folded, like frills on a dress. Try your meaning in the sentence: frilly flaps that are wavy and folded makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Frilly can also mean fancy, with too much decoration, as in «a frilly speech». Here it is not about cloth at all. The speech is over-decorated, full of fancy words. Always read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: Frilly means decorated with frills, wavy strips of cloth or lace gathered into folds.
fact: You can use frilly to describe frilly dresses, frilly socks and a frilly blouse.
fact: In informal use, frilly means fancy and with too much decoration, as in «a frilly speech».
fact: The frilled lizard of Australia spreads a frilly neck to scare its enemies.
fact: Frillier and frilliest are the comparative and superlative forms of frilly.
exercise: «Some lie on the seabed looking like a frilly carpet.» What does frilly describe? | Smooth and flat | Very heavy | *Wavy, folded edges | Hot and dry
exercise: The frilled lizard spreads a frilly neck to scare enemies. What is the neck like? | *Covered in wavy, folded skin like a frill | Thin like a piece of string | Smooth and shiny like glass
exercise: Dad says the speech was frilly, full of fancy words and decoration. What does frilly mean here? | *Fancy, with too much decoration | Wet and muddy | Short and plain | Quiet and calm
test: «Her frilly blouse had lace around the collar.» What does frilly describe? | *Wavy strips of cloth gathered into folds | Something very cold | A tall, thin tree
test: «Wobbegongs are flat sharks with patterned skin and frilly flaps around the mouth.» What are the frilly flaps like? | Smooth like glass | Thin like wire | Hard and sharp like rocks | *Wavy and folded, like frills
exam: Frilly changes form to show more. What is the superlative of frilly? | more frilly | frillish | frillest | *frilliest
